{"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Aptabase","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Aptabase"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"text":" makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for Aptabase in one call. It checks your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key and takes the region from it: an ","type":"text"},{"code":"A-EU-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" key posts to ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/eu.aptabase.com\/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"A-US-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" key to ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/us.aptabase.com\/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a self-hosted ","type":"text"},{"code":"A-SH-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" key to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" under the ","type":"text"},{"code":"host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" you pass. The key goes in each request’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"App-Key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header field,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder"},{"text":" writes the body. Each batch is split to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":": 25 events a request, the most Aptabase takes, and 1,000,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, under the 1 MiB that nginx takes by default in front of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many self-hosted servers. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and also 418, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Aptabase answers when a request’s body arrives slower than 60 bytes a second after a 10-second","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"grace period, as over a poor connection (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"},{"text":"). It drops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out, so import","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What Aptabase does with these events depends on more than the events themselves:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase counts users itself. Its server hashes each request’s IP address and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User-Agent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header field with a salt it changes every day, so a user is one network address and client on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one day. The destination sends no user or device identifier; it can’t keep the server from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seeing the address a request comes from."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase looks up each request’s IP address and stores its country and region with every event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the request, so its dashboard breaks counts down by where the requests came from.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Its sessions are the sessions enricher’s. A record with no session, from a tracker without the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enricher, counts as a session of one event. A record a store recovered after a relaunch keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its session.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its breakdowns by operating system, app version, build, device model and locale come from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context. Give the tracker the standard context enrichers, or those breakdowns are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty. A recovered record keeps only the session of its context, so it shows none of them."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"type":"text","text":" decides where events go. Aptabase shows events marked as debug events only in its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Debug mode, apart from your users’ events, and keeps them for months rather than years."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase requires an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdkVersion"},{"text":" with every event, and keeps it, but its events dashboard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t show it. The destination always sends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app key is public, as Aptabase’s own SDKs ship it inside every app, and the events API takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no other credential, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import AptabaseEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let aptabase = try HTTPDestination.aptabase(","    appKey: appKey,  \/\/ from the app's Instructions page: A-EU-…, A-US-… or A-SH-…","    isDebug: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose events only Debug mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: aptabase)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For a self-hosted server, pass the URL it is reached at as ","type":"text"},{"code":"host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/aptabase.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with a path where it is served under one; the destination appends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A host must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": for a key that is empty or only whitespace; for one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-"},{"type":"text","text":", a region, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" and a body of ASCII letters and digits; for a region other than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EU"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"US"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SH"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEV"},{"type":"text","text":", in capitals; for a self-hosted key without a host, or a cloud key with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one; and for a host that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, or that already ends in the endpoint. A key of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a server run in development ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-DEV-"},{"type":"text","text":") is taken as a self-hosted one, so it needs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"development server’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"host"},{"type":"text","text":": Aptabase’s SDKs default to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/localhost:3000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for such a key, which the factory refuses, so serve the development server over TLS. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"type":"text","text":" has no default:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for builds whose events only Debug mode should show, such as debug builds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Sessions","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Sessions"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher: its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a lowercase UUID. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account, and no trace context. A record with no session has its own identifier as its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":": making up a session would join unrelated records, skipping the record would lose it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Aptabase takes no event without a session."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-Aptabase-receives","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Aptabase receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a JSON array of events. Every event has:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventName"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s name;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sessionId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the session;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so an event sent late still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counts at the time it was tracked;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"systemProps"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osName"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osVersion"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appVersion"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appBuildNumber"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceModel"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"},{"text":", the locale’s language and region (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"text":"), each when the record’s context has it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"text":", as you pass it; and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdkVersion"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"text":". A context value longer than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of its version, 50 of the app’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model) is left out and the event is sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it, as Aptabase would refuse the whole request. A long build number such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026.11.27.1432-abc1234"},{"text":" is left out of every event the build sends, so its breakdown is empty.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each one;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"props"},{"type":"text","text":", when the event has any to send."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made with. Aptabase keeps strings, numbers and booleans, and only a placeholder for an object or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an array, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart"},{"text":" holding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart.size"},{"text":", and the first element of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags.0"},{"text":". A boolean stays a boolean, which Aptabase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":"; a number keeps its JSON type; and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" property is left out. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase stores a number as a .NET ","type":"text"},{"code":"decimal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it keeps 28 decimal places and rounds a smaller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fraction away.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name is only whitespace or longer than the 60 characters Aptabase takes, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase refuses the whole request holding one;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a property, once flattened, whose name is empty, only whitespace or longer than 40"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters, which Aptabase would drop;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a string value longer than 180 characters, which Aptabase would cut short;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a number of magnitude 2⁹⁶ (about 7.9 × 10²⁸) or more, past a ","type":"text"},{"code":"decimal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", for which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Aptabase fails the whole request;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one tracked more than 23 hours before its batch is encoded, as Aptabase drops an event more than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a day old while answering 200, the hour to spare for a queue on the server and clocks that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disagree;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one too large for a request of 1,000,000 bytes on its own.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Characters are counted in UTF-16, as .NET counts them, so an emoji counts two. The destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports each record left out as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request is encoded once and retried as it is, so each request’s deadline is 23 hours after its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest record was tracked: one still failing by then, a slow upload’s 418 included, isn’t sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, which Aptabase would answer with 200 while storing nothing. It is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":". A clock that reads NaN or infinite has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every record reported. An event from the future, by a clock that runs ahead, is sent, and Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores it at the time it arrives."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The 23 hours are measured by the device’s own clock, but Aptabase measures a day by its server’s.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"On a device whose clock runs about a day behind, a record tracked just now carries a timestamp a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"day old: the encoder sends it, and Aptabase drops it while answering 200, so the record is lost","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without a report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-Aptabases-answers-say","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Aptabase’s answers say"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase answers 200 to a request with a key of no app, of a deleted app, or of an account it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"locked, such as one past its plan’s monthly events, and stores nothing. Its body says so,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":", so the destination drops the request and reports it as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":", with Aptabase’s error as the reason."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Every request is refused that way until the key is fixed or the account unlocked, so watch the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drop reports, and check that the first events reach the app’s Live View after setting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination up. It doesn’t remove duplicates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a store’s redelivery, is counted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"twice."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase takes 20 requests a second from one IP address, and answers 429 past it, which the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination retries on its backoff.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Aptabase receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AptabaseEncoding"}],"title":"AptabaseEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"AptabaseEncoding","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"references":{"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/AptabaseBatchEncoder/transientStatuses":{"url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder\/transientstatuses","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transientStatuses","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15TransientStatusV","text":"TransientStatus","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"transientStatuses","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The status Aptabase answers that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries, beside 408, 429 and every 5xx:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"418, which Aptabase answers when a request’s body arrives slower than 60 bytes a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after a 10-second grace period, as over a poor connection."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","title":"AptabaseEncoding","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API."}],"type":"topic","role":"c